kx puts the app in this folder on Kubernetix.

Examples:
  kx deploy                build this folder and put it live (logs in first if needed)
  kx status                see what's live
  kx logs --follow         watch your app's output
  kx open                  open your app in the browser

Usage:
  kx [flags]
  kx <command>

Get started:
  deploy      Build this folder and put it live
  status      See what's live: version, URL, replicas, deploys left today
  logs        Show your app's output
  rollback    Put the previous version back
  open        Open your app in the browser

More commands:
  apps        List and inspect apps
  link        Choose the app this folder deploys to
  login       Connect this computer to Kubernetix
  logout      Revoke this computer's token and forget it
  token       List and revoke API tokens
  whoami      Show where this computer is logged in
  version     Show which kx this is

Options:
  -h, --help      help for kx
      --json      print machine-readable JSON
      --org org   use this org (default: the folder's, then your last login)

More about a command: kx <command> --help
